+# Windows store slice status
+
+Stopped before implementation at the cross-logon mutex security requirement. A `Local\\` mutex would not protect locally persistent credentials across sessions. The global-mutex design needs a verified current-user SID ACL and object-creation policy before safely proceeding.
+
+No product code changed, no tests/checks were run, and no native Windows behavior is claimed. See [windows-store-evidence.md](/home/abdel/Documents/Coding/binus-cli/.agent/windows-store-evidence.md) for the API review, sources, and remaining blockers. Existing browser/process/signal Windows compile failures remain separate and are documented in [windows-portability-evidence.md](/home/abdel/Documents/Coding/binus-cli/.agent/windows-portability-evidence.md).

